mainmenu "SCI latency tester"

config SCI_LATENCY_CENTRAL
	bool "Run as the SCI latency Central (else Peripheral)"
	help
	  When set, this build is the Central: it connects, drives the link to a
	  1.25 ms connection interval via the LE Connection Rate Update procedure,
	  sweeps the subrate factor and logs round-trip GATT latency over the VCOM
	  UART. When unset, this build is the Peripheral that advertises and accepts.

config SCI_LATENCY_ECV_SWEEP
	bool "ECV: sweep the sub-1.25 ms band 1125..375 us (find the HW floor)"
	depends on SCI_LATENCY_CENTRAL
	help
	  Instead of a fixed 1.25 ms interval + subrate sweep, start just below the
	  known-good RCV 1.25 ms and drive the link down the whole ECV (Extended
	  Connection Interval Values) band -- 1125, 1000, 875, 750, 625, 500, 375 us --
	  at subrate factor 1, measuring round-trip GATT latency at each and stopping at
	  the first interval the silicon cannot sustain. This finds the hardware floor
	  wherever it is: bsim (idealised radio) held 750/625 us, but real single-timer
	  silicon (cumulative drift + on-air margin at the standard 150 us tIFS) may
	  floor higher -- which the idealised bsim radio model cannot reproduce.

config SCI_LATENCY_PLAIN_SUBRATE
	bool "Control: plain subrating at 7.5 ms (no SCI / Connection Rate Update)"
	depends on SCI_LATENCY_CENTRAL
	help
	  Isolation control. Instead of the SCI Connection Rate Update to 1.25 ms,
	  the Central does a standard LE connection parameter update to a 7.5 ms
	  interval (BT_HCI_LE_INTERVAL_MIN, no SCI involved) and then sweeps the
	  subrate factor. This exercises only the original subrating path, so a clean
	  factor*interval result here vs a high floor on the 1.25 ms SCI build
	  pinpoints whether the latency is the SCI interaction or subrating itself.

config SCI_LATENCY_PLAIN_INTERVAL_UNITS
	int "Plain-subrate connection interval (1.25 ms units)"
	depends on SCI_LATENCY_PLAIN_SUBRATE
	default 6
	help
	  Connection interval for the plain-subrate control, in 1.25 ms units.
	  6 = 7.5 ms (BT_HCI_LE_INTERVAL_MIN). 24 = 30 ms (matches the conn_subrate
	  bsim test's CONN_INTERVAL_UNITS, for an apples-to-apples HW-vs-bsim run).

config SCI_LATENCY_IDLE_GAP_MS
	int "Idle inter-read gap (ms)"
	depends on SCI_LATENCY_CENTRAL
	default 200
	help
	  Gap between isolated ("idle") reads. Must exceed the subrate skip period so
	  the peer re-sleeps between reads. bsim uses 400 ms.

config SCI_LATENCY_BURST_GAP_MS
	int "Burst inter-read gap (ms)"
	depends on SCI_LATENCY_CENTRAL
	default 2
	help
	  Gap between back-to-back ("burst") reads. Must stay inside the continuation
	  (awake) window = (factor-1) * interval, so the gap has to scale with the
	  interval: ~2 ms at 1.25 ms, 50 ms at 30 ms (bsim's value).

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
